{{!-- The foot of every Surface, in the two shapes the design draws.

	{{> "chrome/footer"}}              the full foot: mark, two menus, the newsletter
	{{> "chrome/footer" slim=true}}    one row, for Surfaces the full foot would outweigh

The design draws four columns and fills two of them with link lists it wrote by hand. A
publication has exactly two menus it can edit, so those are the two columns: the primary menu
under "Sections" and the secondary one under "More". Nothing here is a hardcoded link — a
buyer who empties a menu loses its column, and the grid re-flows, which is the honest
outcome. An RSS link is a menu item like any other; add /rss/ to the secondary menu and it
appears in the footer.

The newsletter column is Ghost's own signup form: `data-members-form` on the form and
`data-members-email` on the input are the whole contract, and Portal — already on the page out of
{{ghost_head}} — binds the submit, posts the magic link and reports back on the form element. Read
out of portal 2.71 rather than from docs, which matters because the class set is narrower than it
looks: the handler clears `success`, `invalid` and `error`, then adds `loading` for the round trip
and exactly one of `success` or `error` at the end. It never adds `invalid`. Failures also land as
text inside `[data-members-error]`, so that node is a live region, and the sent line is real markup
that CSS reveals rather than a string JavaScript writes. Three rules in assets/css/screen.css are
the whole of the theme's side. It renders only where members exist: a form that cannot sign anyone
up is worse than no form.

The design's bottom-right slot holds the preview tool's own metadata — which layout, which
mode — and neither belongs on a shipped page. The platform attribution takes the slot. --}}
{{#if slim}}
	<footer class="border-border bg-surface border-t">
		<div class="container flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 py-6">
			<span class="text-muted font-mono text-[11.5px]">&copy; {{date format="YYYY"}} {{@site.title}}</span>

			{{!-- Ghost's navigation helper returns an empty string for an empty menu
			(core/frontend/helpers/navigation.js), so the partial never runs and the column
			variant needs no guard of its own — but this wrapper is the theme's, and without
			the guard an emptied secondary menu leaves a labelled landmark holding nothing. --}}
			{{#if @site.secondary_navigation}}
				<nav
					aria-label="{{t "Secondary navigation"}}"
					class="flex flex-wrap gap-5">{{navigation type="secondary" variant="row"}}</nav>
			{{/if}}

			<span class="text-muted font-mono text-[11.5px]">
				<a
					href="https://ghost.org/"
					class="text-muted no-underline">{{t "Powered by Ghost"}}</a>
			</span>
		</div>
	</footer>
{{else}}
	<footer class="border-border bg-surface mt-24 border-t">
		<div class="container grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(190px,100%),1fr))] gap-9 py-14">
			<div>
				{{> "chrome/wordmark" logoHeight="h-4" titleSize="text-[22px]"}}

				{{#if @site.description}}
					<p class="font-ui text-muted mt-3 text-[13.5px] leading-[1.6]">{{@site.description}}</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>

			{{navigation variant="column" heading=(t "Sections")}}

			{{navigation type="secondary" variant="column" heading=(t "More")}}

			{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
				<div>
					<p class="text-muted mb-3.5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Newsletter"}}</p>

					<form
						data-members-form="signup"
						class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
						<label
							for="footer-email"
							class="sr-only">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
						<input
							id="footer-email"
							type="email"
							data-members-email
							required
							autocomplete="email"
							placeholder="{{t "Email"}}"
							class="border-border bg-bg font-ui text-text min-w-0 flex-[1_1_130px] rounded-sm border px-3 py-2.5 text-sm">
						<button
							type="submit"
							class="btn btn-primary font-ui cursor-pointer rounded-sm px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold">{{t "Join"}}</button>

						<p
							data-members-error
							role="alert"
							class="font-ui text-accent w-full text-[12.5px]"></p>
						<p
							role="status"
							class="font-ui text-muted members-sent w-full text-[12.5px]">{{t "Check your inbox for the link."}}</p>
					</form>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		</div>

		<div class="border-border border-t">
			<div class="container flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-4 py-5">
				<span class="text-muted font-mono text-[11.5px]">&copy; {{date format="YYYY"}} {{@site.title}}</span>

				<span class="text-muted font-mono text-[11.5px]">
					<a
						href="https://ghost.org/"
						class="text-muted no-underline">{{t "Powered by Ghost"}}</a>
				</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</footer>
{{/if}}
